  "done": [
   "Phases 0-12 per docs/NETCAP_RESEARCH_LOG.md: data layer with cleaning rules R1-R4 (Abilene) and G1-G4 (GEANT); persistence/ARIMA/seasonal/blend/ridge baselines; LSTM/CNN/CNN-LSTM (residual, original-units MAE loss); horizons 5/30/60 min; link loads and congestion warnings via A; GEANT generalisation; error analysis; DM and day-block bootstrap tests; seasonal inputs; burst fallback rule (k sd) and learned gate; conformal q90 warning margins; rolling-origin folds A/B/C; 3-seed ablations."
  ],
  "key_findings_from_log": [
   "Architecture alone: +0.3-2.5% vs persistence on Abilene (sections 14-15, 19, 23).",
   "Seasonal inputs + fallback rule: +8.7-13.1% vs persistence at 60 min across 4 Abilene folds (section 23.1).",
   "Better forecasts do not give better congestion warnings (sections 16, 22).",
   "GEANT results not robust across folds (section 23.1).",
   "80% utilisation threshold gives zero Abilene events; 50% used (section 16.2)."
  ],
